  "answer": "**Top 5 authors (last 300 commits on `main`)**\n\nThe committer field doesn't identify people here: 299 of 300 commits list `GitHub` as committer, which is what happens when PRs are squash-merged through the web UI. So I ranked by author instead:\n\n1. 翠: 75 commits\n2. btea: 49\n3. andrew: 36\n4. renovate[bot]: 27\n5. github-actions[bot]: 14\n\nIf you want humans only, drop the two bots and the list becomes 翠, btea, andrew, then two more authors I didn't break out.\n\n**Top 5 files changed most often**\n\n1. `pnpm-lock.yaml`: 53 commits\n2. `packages/vite/package.json`: 41\n3. `package.json`: 31\n4. `packages/create-vite/src/index.ts`: 25\n5. `pnpm-workspace.yaml`: 20\n\nMost of the churn is dependency and release bookkeeping, not source logic. Merge commits are excluded from the file counts, but they don't contribute per-file diffs in `git log` anyway.\n\nI cloned the repo with `--depth 300` into `/TMP to get this. The repo is still there if you want to dig further."
